PREAMBLE

This document is the authoritative field reference for the
OOB Guard invention. It serves simultaneously as:

  — A technical disclosure for prior art and prosecution history
  — An operational reference for implementations in any language
    or execution environment
  — A record of the core invariant that defines the invention

The central invariant of this system is stated once here and
applies without exception to every implementation derived from
this disclosure:

  NO CRYPTOGRAPHIC, MEMORY, OR I/O OPERATION MAY CONSUME
  AN EXTERNALLY SUPPLIED LENGTH VALUE WITHOUT EXPLICIT
  VALIDATION, DERIVATION, OR CLAMPING AGAINST AN INTERNALLY
  DEFINED BOUND ESTABLISHED BEFORE THE OPERATION BEGINS.

Everything else in this document is a consequence of that rule.


